Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER (tools 0157): Claude's tabs on a row of their own
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 1003: "如果是claude 的視窗 請分成第三行" (after "檔案和按鈕請分成兩行")
- A Claude Code tab (input.viewType has claudeVSCodePanel) that opens or moves
  in front unpinned is pinned (workbench.action.pinEditor -- it acts on the active
  editor, so only that one; nothing is switched to). At start, the active tab of
  the active group too. activationEvents + onWebviewPanel:claudeVSCodePanel: the
  extension starts when VS Code restores Claude's tabs.
- With this machine's user setting workbench.editor.pinnedTabsOnSeparateRow =
  true: buttons (title bar) / Claude's tabs / file tabs. VS Code puts the pinned
  row first; the order cannot be changed. ht9045Designer.pinClaudeTabs turns it off.

Tests: run_all 3/3 layers (a Claude tab in front pinned -- not a file, a pinned
one, one behind; the setting; the activation event); real VS Code 156/159 (the 3
known stale checks; the selection-timeout set came and went on two runs).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
